  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :<br/>Statement (I) : Dimethyl glyoxime forms a six membered covalent chelate when treated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> solution in presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br/>Statement (II) : Prussian blue precipitate contains iron both in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> oxidation states.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Bf6iK",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Plj8t",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ydg9E",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a0oU1",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Statement I,</p><p>On addition of  <b>dimethylglyoxime</b> (DMG) to nickel ion solution and on adding  little bit of ammonia to make solution basic, it will give a red precipitate. This is a very specific test for nickel <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> cation.</p><p>The reaction is as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>dmg</mi><mo>→</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e875bbfc-2ff1-491f-90e6-5868bb22129b.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 172px;\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> hydrogen bonded chelatesare  formed.</p><p>According to Statement II,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>III</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>II</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Prussian Blue</p><p>IN this complex Fe is  at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>as well as</mtext><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo></math>oxidation state. Where ionisation sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and coordination sphere has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence option A is the answer..</p>",
    "image": null
  },
